hadiths[83]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28026","Narrated Abu Al-Mughirah, narrated Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam Al-Ghassani, he said: narrated Abu Al-Ahwas Hakim ibn Umayr and Habib ibn Ubayd, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you neglect to do a thousand good deeds for Allah when he wakes, saying: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, a hundred times, for they are a thousand good deeds, for he will not do, Allah willing, the like of that in his day of sins, and what he does of good besides that will be abundant."
"28027","Narrated Abu Al-Mughirah, he said: narrated Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, he said: narrated Humayd ibn Uqbah ibn Ruman, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever removes from the path of the Muslims something that harms them, Allah writes a good deed for him thereby, and whoever has a good deed written for him with Him, Allah will admit him to Paradise thereby."
"28028","Narrated Abu Al-Mughirah, he said: narrated Safwan, he said: narrated Shurayh ibn Ubayd Al-Hadrami and others, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam, do not be helpless in four rakahs at the beginning of your day, I will suffice you its end."
"28029","Narrated Abu Al-Mughirah, he said: narrated Safwan, he said: narrated some of the elders, from Abu Idris As-Sakuni, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: My beloved Abu Al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three I will not leave for anything: he advised me to fast three days of each month, and not to sleep except upon witr, and the forenoon glorification prayer in residence and travel."
"28030","Narrated Abu Al-Yaman, he said: narrated Abu Bakr, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah has given you charity of a third of your wealth at your death."
"28031","Narrated Muhammad ibn Musab, he said: narrated Abu Bakr, from Zayd ibn Artah, from one of his brothers, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Everything decreases except evil, for it is increased in."
"28032","Narrated Abu Jafar As-Suwaydi, he said: narrated Abu Ar-Rabi Sulayman ibn Utbah Ad-Dimashqi, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Maysarah, from Abu Idris Aidhullah, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor the believer in magic, nor the addict of wine, nor the denier of decree."
"28033","Narrated Yaqub, he said: narrated my father, from his father, he said: narrated a brother of Adi ibn Artah, from a man, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us that the most fearful of what I fear for you is the misleading leaders."
"28034","Narrated Haytham ibn Kharijah, he said: informed Abu Ar-Rabi Sulayman ibn Utbah As-Sulami, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abu Idris, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If you were forgiven for what you do to cattle, much would be forgiven for you."
"28035","Narrated Haytham, and I heard it myself from Haytham, he said: informed Abu Ar-Rabi, from Yunus, from Abu Idris, from Abu Ad-Darda, they said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us, what we do, is it a matter already completed, or a matter we begin anew? He said: Rather a matter already completed. They said: Then how about deeds, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Every person is prepared for what he was created for."
"28036","Narrated Haytham, and I heard it myself from him, he said: narrated Abu Ar-Rabi, from Yunus, from Abu Idris, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah created Adam when He created him, then struck his right shoulder and brought out white offspring as if they were particles, and struck his left shoulder and brought out black offspring as if they were charred, then said to those in his right: To Paradise, and I do not care, and said to those in his left hand: To the Fire, and I do not care."
"28037","Narrated Haytham, he said: informed Abu Ar-Rabi, from Yunus, from Abu Idris, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection to Adam, peace be upon him: Arise and prepare from your offspring nine hundred ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. So his companions wept and wept, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Raise your heads, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my ummah among the nations is only like a white hair on the skin of a black bull. So that lightened it for them."
"28038","Narrated Haytham, he said: narrated Abu Ar-Rabi, from Yunus, from Abu Idris, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Everything has a reality, and a servant does not reach the reality of faith until he knows that what struck him was never to miss him, and what missed him was never to strike him. Abu Abdur-Rahman said: Al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to me from Abu Ar-Rabi with all these hadiths, except that he stopped one of them, the hadith: If you were forgiven for what you do to cattle, and my father narrated it to us from him as raised."
"28039","Narrated Hasan, he said: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Wahb ibn Abdullah, that Abu Ad-Darda said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, will enter Paradise. He said: I said: Though he fornicate and though he steal? He said: Though he fornicate and though he steal. I said: Though he fornicate and though he steal? He said: Though he fornicate and though he steal. I said: Though he fornicate and though he steal? He said: Though he fornicate and though he steal, despite the nose of Abu Ad-Darda. He said: So I went out to call with it among the people. He said: Then Umar met me and said: Return, for if the people learn of this they will rely on it. So I returned and informed him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Umar spoke truth."
"28040","Narrated Surayj ibn An-Numan, he said: narrated Hushaym, he said: informed Abbad ibn Rashid Al-Minqari, from Al-Hasan and Abu Qilabah, they were sitting, so he said: Abu Qilabah said: Abu Ad-Darda said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately leaves Asr prayer until it escapes him, his deed is nullified."
"28041","Narrated Hasan ibn Musa and Sulayman ibn Harb, they said: narrated Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Bilal ibn Abi Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The green sky has not shaded nor the dusty earth carried one with a tongue more truthful than Abu Dharr."
"28042","Narrated Yahya ibn Ghaylan, he said: narrated Rishdin, he said: narrated Amr ibn Al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar Ad-Dimashqi, that an informant informed him, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, that he said: I prostrated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eleven prostrations, among them the prostration of An-Najm."
"28043","Narrated Sulayman ibn Dawud meaning Abu Dawud At-Tayalisi, he said: narrated Shubah, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad narrating from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night? So it was said: And who can bear that? He said: Recite: Say: He is Allah, One."
"28044","Narrated Abdul-Malik ibn Amr and Ibn Abi Bukayr, they said: narrated Ibrahim meaning Ibn Nafi, from Al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from his uncle Ata ibn Nafi, that they entered upon Umm Ad-Darda, so she informed them that she heard Abu Ad-Darda saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best thing in the balance, Ibn Abi Bukayr said: The heaviest thing in the balance on the Day of Resurrection is good character."
"28045","Narrated Muhammad ibn Bakr, he said: narrated Maymun meaning Abu Muhammad Al-Mirai At-Tamimi, he said: narrated Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: I accompanied Abu Ad-Darda learning from him, so when death came to him he said: Inform the people of my death. So I informed the people of his death, then I came and the house was filled and beyond it. He said: So I said: I have informed the people of your death, and the house is filled and beyond it. He said: Bring me out. So we brought him out. He said: Seat me. So we seated him. He said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects ablution, then prays two rakahs completing them, Allah gives him what he asks, hastened or delayed. Abu Ad-Darda said: O people, beware of turning, for there is no prayer for the one who turns, and if you are overcome in voluntary prayer, then do not be overcome in the obligatory."
"28046","Narrated Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abdul-Wahhab, they said: informed Said, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah Al-Yamuri, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Is one of you not able to recite a third of the Quran in a night? They said: We are weaker than that and more helpless. He said: Allah Almighty divided the Quran into three parts, and made: Say: He is Allah, One, a part of the parts of the Quran."
"28047","Narrated Wahb ibn Jarir, he said: narrated my father, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from Az-Zuhri, that Abu Ad-Darda said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) discussing what will be, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear of a mountain moving from its place, believe it, and if you hear of a man changing from his character, do not believe it, for he will return to what he was formed upon."
"28048","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ubayd, he said: narrated Al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Umm Ad-Darda, she said: Abu Ad-Darda entered upon me while angry, so I said: Who angered you? He said: By Allah, I do not recognize among them anything of the matter of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that they pray together."
"28049","Narrated Abdur-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Umm Ad-Darda, she said: Abu Ad-Darda entered upon me while angry, so I said to him: What is wrong with you? So he said: I do not recognize anything of the matter of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except prayer."
"28050","Narrated Abdus-Samad, he said: narrated my father, he said: narrated Al-Husayn, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: narrated Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr Al-Awzai, from Yaish ibn Al-Walid ibn Hisham, he narrated that his father narrated him, he said: narrated Madan ibn Abi Talhah, that Abu Ad-Darda informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast."
"28051","He said: Then I met Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the mosque of Damascus, so I said: Abu Ad-Darda informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast. He said: He spoke truth, I poured his ablution water for him."
"28052","Narrated Abu Said, he said: informed Abu Yaqub meaning Ishaq ibn Uthman Al-Kilabi, he said: I heard Khalid ibn Durayk narrating from Abu Ad-Darda, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not combine in the belly of a man dust in the path of Allah and smoke of Hell, and whoever has his feet dusted in the path of Allah, Allah forbids the rest of his body to the Fire, and whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances him from the Fire a thousand years journey for the hastening rider, and whoever is wounded a wound in the path of Allah, it is sealed for him with the seal of martyrs, it has light on the Day of Resurrection, its color like the color of saffron and its scent like the scent of musk, the first and the last recognize him by it, saying: So-and-so has the stamp of martyrs upon him, and whoever fights in the path of Allah for the milking of a camel, Paradise is due for him."
"28053","Narrated Hammad ibn Khalid, he said: narrated Hisham ibn Sad, from Uthman ibn Hayyan and Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: We have seen in some of our journeys that one of us would put his hand on his head from severe heat, and none among the people were fasting except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abdullah ibn Rawahah. And Abu Amir said: Uthman ibn Hayyan alone."
"28054","Narrated Waki, he said: narrated Sufyan, from Al-Amash, from Thabit or from Abi Thabit, that a man entered the mosque of Damascus and said: O Allah, comfort my loneliness and have mercy on my strangeness and grant me a beloved righteous companion. So Abu Ad-Darda heard him and said: If you are truthful, I am happier with what you said than you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among them is a wrongdoer to himself, he said: The wrongdoer is taken in his station, so that is worry and grief, and among them is moderate, he is reckoned an easy reckoning, and among them is foremost in good deeds, so those are they who enter Paradise without reckoning."
"28055","Narrated Ali ibn Bahr, he said: narrated Baqiyyah, he said: narrated Thabit ibn Ajlan, he said: narrated Al-Qasim, freedman of Bani Yazid, from Abu Ad-Darda, that a man passed by him while he was planting a plant in Damascus, so he said to him: Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: Do not be hasty with me, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever plants a plant, no human nor any creation of Allah Almighty eats from it except it is charity for him."
"28056","Abdullah said: my father said: Al-Ashjai said, meaning from Sufyan, from Al-Amash, from Abi Ziyad: I entered the mosque of Damascus."
"28057","Narrated Aswad ibn Amir, he said: narrated Israil, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Ad-Darda, do not single out Friday night with standing apart from other nights, nor Friday day with fasting apart from other days."
"28058","Narrated Abu Muawiyah, from Al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of better than the rank of prayer, fasting and charity? They said: Yes. He said: Mending relations, and corruption of relations is the shaver."
"28059","Narrated Abu Muawiyah, he said: narrated Ubaydullah ibn Al-Walid Al-Wassafi, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears a hadith from a man who does not like it to be mentioned from him, it is a trust, even if he did not ask him to keep it secret."
"28060","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, he said: informed Sufyan, from Al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from a man, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about His saying Almighty: For them is glad tidings in the life of the world and in the Hereafter, he said: The righteous dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him."
"28061","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, he said: informed Sufyan, from Ata ibn As-Saib, from Abi Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami, he said: There was among us a man whose mother kept pressing him to marry until he married, then she ordered him to separate from her, so he traveled to Abu Ad-Darda in Sham and said: My mother kept pressing me until I married, then she ordered me to separate. He said: I am not one to order you to separate, nor am I one to order you to keep. I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: The father is the middle gate of Paradise, so waste that gate or preserve it. He said: So he returned, having separated from her."
"28062","Narrated Ali ibn Asim, narrated Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abdullah ibn Yazid As-Sadi, he said: People of my tribe ordered me to ask Said ibn Al-Musayyab about a spear they sharpen and fix in the earth, then morning comes having killed a hyena, do you consider its slaughtering? He said: So I sat with Said ibn Al-Musayyab, and with him was an old man white of head and beard from the people of Sham, so I asked him about that, so he said to me: And do you eat hyena? He said: I said: I never ate it, and people of my tribe eat it. He said: So he said: Eating it is not lawful. He said: So the old man said: O Abdullah, shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from Abu Ad-Darda, he narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I said: Yes. He said: I heard Abu Ad-Darda saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every snatcher, every plunder, every animal kept as a target, and every fanged beast of prey. He said: So Said ibn Al-Musayyab said: He spoke truth."
"28063","Narrated Ali ibn Thabit, narrated Hisham ibn Sad, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, he said: There was a man in Sham called Madan, Abu Ad-Darda used to teach him the Quran, then Abu Ad-Darda missed him, then met him one day at Dabiq, so Abu Ad-Darda said to him: O Madan, what happened to the Quran that was with you, how are you and the Quran today? He said: Allah knew good of it. He said: O Madan, do you live today in a city or a village? He said: No, rather in a village near the city. He said: Wait, woe to you, O Madan, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no five people of houses among whom prayer is not called nor prayers established except Satan overcomes them, and the wolf takes the stray. So keep to the cities, woe to you, O Madan."
"28064","Narrated Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Zaidah ibn Qudamah, and Waki, he said: narrated Zaidah ibn Qudamah, from As-Saib, Waki said: son of Hubaysh Al-Kalai, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah Al-Yamuri, he said: Abu Ad-Darda said to me: Where is your dwelling? He said: I said: In a village below Hims. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no three in a village among whom call is not made nor prayers established except Satan overcomes them. Keep to the congregation, for the wolf only eats the distant one. Ibn Mahdi said: As-Saib said, meaning by congregation prayer."
"28065","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shubah, from Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Umar As-Sini, from Abu Ad-Darda, that when a guest stayed with him, Abu Ad-Darda would say to him: Staying so we saddle, or departing so we feed? He said: If he said to him: departing, he said to him: I find nothing better for you than something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us with. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the rich have gone with reward, they perform pilgrimage and we do not perform pilgrimage, and they strive and we do not strive, and so and so. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to something, if you take it you come with better than what any of them comes with: that you magnify Allah thirty-four times, and glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times at the end of every prayer."
"28066","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj, he said: narrated Shubah, from Qatadah, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad narrating from Madan, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever recites ten verses from the end of Al-Kahf is protected from the trial of Ad-Dajjal. Hajjaj said: Whoever recites the last ten of Surah Al-Kahf."
"28067","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shubah, he said: I heard Al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata Al-KaykharanI, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is heavier in the balance than good character."
"28068","Narrated it to us Yazid, he said: informed Shubah, from Al-Kaykharani."
"28069","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shubah, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrating from his father, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by a pregnant woman at the door of a tent, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps he wants to approach her. So they said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him: How does he make him inherit though it is not lawful for him, how does he use him as a servant though it is not lawful for him."
"28070","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shubah, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Ata ibn Yasar, from an elder, from Abu Ad-Darda, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this verse: Those who believed and were God-fearing, for them is glad tidings in the life of the world, he said: The righteous dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him."
"28071","Narrated Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Al-Munkadir, he heard it from Ata ibn Yasar, and Abdul-Aziz ibn Rufay from Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of the people of Egypt: I asked Abu Ad-Darda, then he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similar."
"28072","Narrated Bahz, narrated Bukayr ibn Abi As-Sumayt, narrated Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad Al-Ghatafani, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah Al-Yamuri, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran each day? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are weaker than that and more helpless. He said: Allah divided the Quran into three parts, so: Say: He is Allah, One, is a part of its parts."
"28073","And narrated it to us Affan, narrated Aban, narrated Qatadah, from Salim, from Madan, from Abu Ad-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite, then he mentioned its meaning."
"28074","My father said: and Affan said: narrated Bukayr ibn Abi As-Sumayt with this chain likewise."
"28075","Narrated Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, narrated Abu Mashar, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, freedman of Ibn Ayyash, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds, and the purest of them with your King, and the highest of them in your ranks, and better for you than giving gold and silver, and better for you than meeting your enemy so you strike their necks and they strike your necks: remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"28076","Narrated Abu Muawiyah, he said: narrated Al-Amash, from Abi Salih, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of the people of Egypt, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: A man came to him and said: What do you say about the saying of Allah: For them is glad tidings in the life of the world and in the Hereafter? He said: You asked about something no one asked about after a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: Their glad tidings in the life of the world is the righteous dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him, and their glad tidings in the Hereafter is Paradise."
"28077","Narrated Ibn Numayr, narrated Al-Amash, from Abi Salih, from Abu Ad-Darda, like the hadith of Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever of my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, except that in it is: though the nose of Abu Ad-Darda is rubbed in dust."
"28078","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, informed Sufyan, from Ata ibn As-Saib, from Abi Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami, he said: There was among us a man, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: So he traveled to Abu Ad-Darda and said: I heard the Prophet saying: The father is the middle gate of Paradise."
"28079","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, narrated Mamar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: Abdul-Malik ibn Marwan used to send to Umm Ad-Darda, so she would stay overnight with his women, and he would ask her about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he stood one night and called his servant, so she was slow with him, so he cursed her. So she said: Do not curse, for Abu Ad-Darda narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The frequent cursers will not be witnesses nor intercessors on the Day of Resurrection."
"28080","Narrated Zayd ibn Al-Hubab, narrated Muawiyah ibn Salih, narrated Abu Az-Zahiriyyah Hudayr ibn Kurayb, from Kathir ibn Murrah Al-Hadrami, he said: I heard Abu Ad-Darda saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there recitation in every prayer? He said: Yes. So a man of the Ansar said: This is obligatory. So Abu Ad-Darda turned to me, and I was the nearest of the people to him, and said: O son of my brother, I do not see the imam when he leads the people except that he suffices them."
"28081","Narrated Yahya ibn Said, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, that Muawiyah bought a silver water vessel for less than its price or more. He said: So Abu Ad-Darda said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the like of this except like for like."
"28082","Narrated Yahya ibn Said, from Shubah, he said: narrated Al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata Al-Kaykharani, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing is heavier in the balance than good character."
"28083","Narrated Waki, narrated Sufyan, and Abdur-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Habibah At-Tai, from Abu Ad-Darda, Abdur-Rahman said in his hadith: So I met Abu Ad-Darda, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of one who frees at death is like the example of one who gives a gift when full."
"28084","Narrated Waki, narrated Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abi As-Safar, he said: A man of Quraysh broke the tooth of a man of the Ansar, so he sought justice against him from Muawiyah. So the Qurashi said: This one struck my tooth. Muawiyah said: No, we will please him. He said: When the Ansari insisted upon him, Muawiyah said: Deal with your companion as you wish, and Abu Ad-Darda was sitting. So Abu Ad-Darda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim is struck in his body with something then gives it as charity except Allah raises him a degree thereby and removes a sin from him thereby. He said: So the Ansari said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, my ears heard it and my heart retained it, meaning so he pardoned him."
"28085","Narrated Ismail, narrated Dawud, and Ibn Abi Adi, from Dawud, from Ash-Shabi, from Alqamah, he said: I met Abu Ad-Darda, Ibn Abi Adi said in his hadith: So I came to Sham and met Abu Ad-Darda. He said: From whom are you? I said: From the people of Kufah. He said: Do you recite to me the recitation of Ibn Masud? I said: Yes. He said: So recite: By the night when it covers. I said: By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines, and the male and the female. He said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it. He said, I think he said: So he laughed."
"28086","Narrated Ismail, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever defends the honor of his Muslim brother, it is due upon Allah Almighty to defend him from the Fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."
"28087","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, narrated Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn Al-Walid, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast, so water was brought and he performed ablution."
"28088","Narrated Yazid ibn Harun, informed Shubah, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that he came to Sham and entered the mosque of Damascus, then prayed in it two rakahs and said: O Allah, grant me a righteous companion. He said: So he came and sat with Abu Ad-Darda. So Abu Ad-Darda said to him: From whom are you? He said: From the people of Kufah. He said: How did you hear Ibn Umm Abd reciting: By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines? Alqamah said: And the male and the female. So Abu Ad-Darda said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and these people kept at me until they made me doubt. Then he said: Was there not among you the companion of the cushion and the companion of the secret which none knows but him, and the one granted refuge from Satan upon the tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the companion of the cushion is Ibn Masud, and the companion of the secret is Hudhayfah, and the one granted refuge from Satan is Ammar."
"28089","Narrated Affan, narrated Shubah, he said: informed Mughirah, he said: I heard Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah went to Sham, then he mentioned the hadith."
"28090","Narrated Rawh, narrated Said, from Qatadah, narrated Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad Al-Ghatafani, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah Al-Yamuri, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surah Al-Kahf is protected from the trial of Ad-Dajjal."
"28091","Narrated Husayn, in the Tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, he said: narrated Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Ad-Darda, then he mentioned likewise."
"28092","Narrated Abdus-Samad and Affan, they said: narrated Hammam, Affan said in his hadith: narrated Hammam, he said: Qatadah used to narrate it to us, he said: narrated Salim ibn Abi Al-Jad Al-Ghatafani, from the hadith of Madan ibn Abi Talhah Al-Yamuri, from the hadith of Abu Ad-Darda, he narrating from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned likewise. Then he returned to the hadith of Abdus-Samad, he said: narrated Hammam, narrated Qatadah, from Salim, from the hadith of Madan, from Abu Ad-Darda, he narrating from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever memorizes ten verses of Surah Al-Kahf."
"28093","Narrated Ali ibn Ishaq, informed Abdullah meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: informed Abu Bakr An-Nahshali, from Marzuq Abu Bakr At-Taymi, from Umm Ad-Darda, from Abu Ad-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever defends the honor of his brother, Allah defends the Fire from his face on the Day of Resurrection."
"28094","Narrated Aswad ibn Amir, narrated Israil, from Al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I came to Sham and entered the mosque and prayed two rakahs and said: O Allah, make easy for me a righteous companion, then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Shubah."
"28095","Narrated Abu Al-Ala Al-Hasan ibn Sawwar, narrated Layth, from Muawiyah, from Abi Halbas Yazid ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Umm Ad-Darda saying: I heard Abu Ad-Darda saying: I heard Abu Al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, I did not hear him use his kunyah before it nor after it, saying: Allah Almighty says: O Isa, I am sending after you a nation, if what they love befalls them they praise Allah and thank, and if what they dislike befalls them they reckon and are patient, with neither forbearance nor knowledge. He said: O Lord, how is this for them with neither forbearance nor knowledge? He said: I give them of My forbearance and My knowledge."
"28096","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abdul-Malik, narrated Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl, he said: narrated Kathir Abu Al-Fadl At-Tufawi, narrated Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: I came to Abu Ad-Darda in his illness in which he died, so he said to me: O son of my brother, what brought you purposely to this land, or what brought you? He said: I said: Nothing but keeping ties of what was between you and my father Abdullah ibn Salam. So Abu Ad-Darda said: This is a bad hour of lying, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects ablution, then stands and prays two or four rakahs, Sahl doubted, performing remembrance and humility well in them, then seeks forgiveness of Allah Almighty, He forgives him."
"28097","Abdullah said: and narrated it to us Said ibn Abi Ar-Rabi As-Samman, he said: narrated Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl Al-Hunai, Abdullah said: and Ahmad ibn Abdul-Malik erred in the name of the sheikh, so he said: Sahl ibn Abi Sadaqah, but it is Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl Al-Hunai."
"28098","Narrated Affan, narrated Hammam, he said: narrated Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abi Salih, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that when death came to him he said: Admit the people to me. So they were admitted to him. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, Allah places him in Paradise. And I would not have narrated it to you except at death. And the witness to that is Uwaymir Abu Ad-Darda. So they came to Abu Ad-Darda, so he said: My brother spoke truth, and he would not narrate it to you except at his death."
"28099","Narrated Muhammad ibn Musab, narrated Abu Bakr, from Khalid ibn Muhammad, from Bilal ibn Abi Ad-Darda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your love of a thing blinds and deafens."
"28100","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shubah, from Mughirah, that he heard Ibrahim narrating, he said: Alqamah came to Sham and prayed two rakahs, then said: O Allah, grant me a righteous companion. He said: So I sat with a man, and he was Abu Ad-Darda. So he said: From whom are you? So I said: From the people of Kufah. So he said: Do you know how Abdullah used to recite this letter: By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines, and He created the male and the female? So I said: He used to recite it: By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines, and the male and the female. So he said: Thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it, and these people kept at me until they almost made me doubt. Then he said: Is there not among you the companion of the cushion and the siwak, meaning Abdullah ibn Masud, is there not among you the one Allah granted refuge upon the tongue of His Prophet from Satan, meaning Ammar ibn Yasir, is there not among you the one who knows the secret and none other knows it, meaning Hudhayfah."
"28101","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Shurayh ibn Ubayd, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: Son of Adam, do not fail in four rakahs at the beginning of the day, I will suffice you its end."
"28102","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Sakuni, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, he said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three things I will not leave for anything: he advised me with fasting three days of every month, and not to sleep except after witr, and the forenoon prayer while resident and traveling."
"28103","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata meaning Ibn al-Saib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, he said: Abu al-Darda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The father is the middle gate of Paradise, so guard that gate or leave it."
"28104","Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Yala ibn Mamlak, on the authority of Umm al-Darda, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, raising it to the Prophet: Whoever is given his share of gentleness is given his share of good, and there is nothing heavier in the Scale than good character."
"28105","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: We came to Sham and Abu al-Darda came to us and said: Is there among you one who recites to me the recitation of Abdullah? They pointed to me. He said: I said: Yes, I. He said: How did you hear Abdullah recite this verse, By the night when it covers and the day when it shines? He said: I said: I heard him recite, By the night when it covers and the day when it shines and the male and the female. He said: And I, by Allah, thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite it, and these want me to recite, and what He created, but I do not follow them."
"28106","Sufyan narrated to us another time, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Yala ibn Mamlak, on the authority of Umm al-Darda, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The heaviest thing in the Scale on the Day of Resurrection is good character."
"28107","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ata ibn Yasar, on the authority of a man of the people of Egypt, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, he said: He was asked about this verse, For them is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. He said: You have asked about something I have not heard anyone ask about after a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: It is the righteous dream which the Muslim man sees or which is seen for him, his glad tidings in the life of this world, and his glad tidings in the Hereafter is Paradise."
"28108","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qurdusi narrated to us, on the authority of Qays ibn Sad, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, on the authority of Abu al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the wealth of the ruler, and he said: Whatever Allah brings you of it without asking and without aspiring, eat it and take it as wealth. He said: And al-Hasan said: There is no harm in it so long as he does not journey to it or aspire for it."
